# action — ActionTarget / LpExecutor / GroupActionExecutor / GroupServiceExecutor.
#
# No numeric parameter is configured here any more. Until ../action 652c270, GroupActionExecutor
# took a `uint256[] splits` constructor argument (the verification-open schedule: rank 1 opens at the
# start of the verification phase, rank k>=2 at splits[k-2]); that schedule has been removed from the
# contract, so the constructor is now `(actionTarget)` only and GROUP_ACTION_SPLITS is gone from this
# file, script/DeployLocal.s.sol, script/export.py, script/verify.sh and the exported
# `params.groupActionSplits` key. Do not re-add it unless the sibling repo reintroduces the concept.
#
# The four GroupActionExecutor / GroupServiceExecutor libraries are NOT configured here: their
# addresses are compile-time link targets, so they cannot come from a params file that is read after
# compilation. script/DeployLibraries.s.sol deploys them first, script/local.sh reads the resulting
# addresses out of that run's broadcast JSON, and the addresses are passed to `forge script
# --libraries` and exported to export/deployments/anvil31337_dev.json (address book keys
# GROUP_ACTION_JOIN_LIBRARY_ADDRESS and friends). See README "Linked libraries".
